## 1. Channels Inventory (Current State)
- **Website:** [triathlon.ky](https://www.triathlon.ky/) — built on Squarespace. Intended role: informational hub covering events, volunteering, coaching, and youth programs (not a transaction/sign-up site). Newsletter signup block on homepage is **not configured with a storage location**, so sign-ups may not be captured — worth fixing regardless of the site's hub role. Last updated: unknown. Access/ownership: unknown — needs confirming.
- **Membership/registration:** Handled via a separate site, [racecaribbean.net](https://racecaribbean.net/shop/memberships/cayman-islands-triathlon-association-annual-membership/), run by a fellow board member — this split (triathlon.ky = info hub, racecaribbean.net = sign-up) is intentional. **Future goal:** stand up our own Cayman Triathlon membership covering annual insurance plus added benefits (discounts at shops/races, access to coaching/training events) — see Section 8.
- **Social media:**
  - Facebook: [CaymanIslandsTriathlonAssociation](https://www.facebook.com/CaymanIslandsTriathlonAssociation/) — ~1.4k followers. Posting is irregular, loosely tied to events, no consistent cadence.
  - Instagram: [@cayman_triathlon](https://www.instagram.com/cayman_triathlon/?hl=en) — 193 followers, 15 posts total, **nothing posted since 2016**.
  - Twitter/X: [@CaymanTriathlon](https://twitter.com/CaymanTriathlon) — 177 followers, **no posts since 2019**, effectively dormant.
  - Reason for dormancy (per board president): deprioritized as available resources diminished, not a deliberate strategic retirement.
  - Direction: **revive all three channels**, with a distinct plan per platform (not a copy-paste approach across them).
  - Manager(s) for each platform: unknown — needs confirming.
- **Email/newsletter:** Sent via Mailchimp. List size, send frequency, and content owner: unknown — needs confirming. (See website finding above — signup form issue may be limiting list growth.)
- **Print/physical:** Every event has its own race-day signage, sponsor boards, and flyers (designed per-event, not from a shared template/system). Additional physical media — t-shirts, hats, medals — design/ownership process unknown.
- **Press/media relations:** Unclear — no known local news contacts or record of past coverage. Needs investigating.

## 2. Brand & Messaging Consistency
- Logo/brand guidelines: **No single consistent logo.** Facebook's logo matches the website; Instagram uses a different logo. Facebook and the website are the most up-to-date and should be the reference point going forward. **No known brand guideline document exists — needs confirming.** A guideline should be created covering: correct logo usage, color palette + how to apply it, and typography/fonts.
- Tone/voice: Currently unclear/inconsistent — hard to assess with so little recent posting (esp. Instagram, dormant since 2016). Goal: consistency across channels and events so everything feels recognizably "Cayman Triathlon," while allowing intentional flexibility — different events can target different audiences and have slight tonal differences on top of the shared base identity.
- Photo/video asset library: Unknown whether one currently exists — needs confirming. Also need to define, going forward: where photos/videos/documents are stored, and usage guidance (what photos can be used for, any restrictions).
- Physical/merch branding (t-shirts, hats, medals): Design process and level of consistency unknown — needs confirming, including whether design is sponsor-determined.

## 3. Content & Cadence
- Current posting cadence: Website — events added as they become known. Facebook — updates posted as events happen (reactive, not scheduled). No consistent cadence beyond this. Newsletter cadence unknown — needs confirming.
- Event promotion timeline: **None currently.** No defined pre/during/post-race promotion process — content goes up as events happen rather than being planned in advance.
- Volunteer recruitment: **No clear, consistent call-out for volunteers across any platform.**
- Gaps:
  - Instagram and Twitter/X are effectively dead channels (see Section 1)
  - Some events are missing from the Facebook page entirely
  - No event promotion timeline/plan exists
  - No structured volunteer messaging

## 4. Audience & Engagement
- Audience size/demographics per channel:
  - Instagram: 193 followers, 15 posts total, nothing posted since 2016
  - Twitter/X: 177 followers, nothing posted since 2019
  - Facebook: 1.4k followers — posted about the most recent event (Stoke and Stride), but nothing before that since November 2025
  - Website: up to date with event listings, but **not up to date with current board member info**. Newsletter signup link appears broken (consistent with Section 1 finding).
  - No demographic breakdown available for any channel — needs confirming (Meta/Instagram insights, if accessible, would give this for FB/IG).
- Engagement quality: **No engagement metrics currently tracked** (likes, comments, shares, click-throughs, sign-ups driven by posts, etc.)
- Member/participant feedback: **None collected.**
- Direction: focus on growing these platforms, and start measuring engagement — with a specific eye on how engagement translates into real-world outcomes (event participation, volunteer sign-ups), not just follower counts.

